BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL 56 760 Td (Vacancy Atlas) Tj T* () Tj T* (Vacancy Atlas: Executive Summary) Tj T* () Tj T* (Problem) Tj T* () Tj T* (Small cities face a difficult problem when they try to revitalize their downtowns and) Tj T* (neighborhoods. They often do not know how many storefronts and homes are actually vacant, or) Tj T* (where the vacancies are concentrated. Without that information, it is hard to decide where to) Tj T* (spend limited revitalization funds. A planner in a small city may rely on a windshield survey) Tj T* (done by an intern, a list from the assessor that is a year or two old, or the personal) Tj T* (knowledge of a long-serving staff member. These approaches are slow, expensive in staff time,) Tj T* (and inconsistent from one year to the next.) Tj T* () Tj T* (The stakes are real. Federal and state programs, as well as private foundations, offer funding) Tj T* (for revitalization, but most of them ask applicants to show need with data. Cities that cannot) Tj T* (document their vacancy levels are at a disadvantage when applying. Cities that do receive funds) Tj T* (often cannot show afterward whether the money made a difference, because they never had a) Tj T* (baseline.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Solution) Tj T* () Tj T* (Vacancy Atlas is a data product that estimates vacant storefronts and homes by cross-) Tj T* (referencing two kinds of signals: utility activity and mail-delivery status. When a property) Tj T* (has had no active utility account or very low usage for an extended period, and mail-delivery) Tj T* (records flag it as undeliverable or vacant, the likelihood that it is empty is high. Neither) Tj T* (signal is perfect alone, but together they give a more reliable picture than either one. Our) Tj T* (software combines them, assigns each property a vacancy likelihood score, and displays the) Tj T* (results on an easy-to-read map with block-level summaries.) Tj T* () Tj T* (The output is designed for non-technical users. A planner can open the map, filter by) Tj T* (neighborhood or property type, and export a list for grant applications or field verification.) Tj T* (We also provide a short quarterly update so that cities can track change over time.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Market) Tj T* () Tj T* (Our target customers are municipal planning and economic development offices in small and mid-) Tj T* (sized cities, which we define as roughly 20,000 to 150,000 residents. In the United States) Tj T* (there are several hundred such cities in the regions where we plan to start. We also see) Tj T* (regional planning councils, downtown development authorities, and community development) Tj T* (nonprofits as possible buyers. Many of these organizations manage grant programs and need data) Tj T* (to decide where to send funds.) Tj T* () Tj T* (We estimate that if we reach a modest share of these organizations at an annual price in the) Tj T* (low thousands of dollars each, the market is large enough to support a small company. We) Tj T* (recognize that this estimate is rough and that municipal budgets are tight. We plan to refine) Tj T* (it through conversations with pilot customers.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Business Model) Tj T* () Tj T* (We plan to sell annual subscriptions. The base subscription would include access to the vacancy) Tj T* (map, a yearly data refresh, and exports. A higher tier would add quarterly updates and help) Tj T* (with grant applications. We expect pricing to depend on the size of the city. Early pilots may) Tj T* (be offered at a discount or free in exchange for feedback and permission to describe results.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Our costs are mainly data acquisition, cloud hosting, and the time of the founders. The biggest) Tj T* (uncertainty is access to the underlying data. We are exploring agreements with utility) Tj T* (providers and using publicly available delivery-status information, and we are working through) Tj T* (what privacy rules require. We believe that aggregating to the property level without personal) Tj T* (information keeps us on safe ground, but we plan to get legal advice before expanding.) Tj ET
endstream
