BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL 56 760 Td () Tj T* (Competition) Tj T* () Tj T* (The space is crowded. Large data companies sell property and demographic data to cities, and) Tj T* (some include vacancy indicators. Several software firms offer planning and permitting platforms) Tj T* (that touch on vacancy. Some cities build their own tools using in-house analysts or university) Tj T* (partners, and many simply use spreadsheets and field surveys. Our advantage is that we focus) Tj T* (only on vacancy and design for small cities that cannot afford large platforms or dedicated) Tj T* (data staff. Our use of utility and mail signals is not unique in principle, but we believe our) Tj T* (focus on simplicity, price, and small-city needs gives us a place in the market. We know that) Tj T* (larger competitors could add similar features, and we will need to move quickly to build) Tj T* (relationships.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Team) Tj T* () Tj T* (Marcus Delgado leads product and customer relations. He is studying urban planning at our) Tj T* (university and has worked part time in a city planning office, where he saw the vacancy problem) Tj T* (firsthand. Priya Raman is responsible for data and modeling. She studies statistics and built) Tj T* (the first version of our scoring approach. Tobias Lindqvist handles software development and) Tj T* (the map interface; he is a computer science student with experience building web applications.) Tj T* (Together we cover planning knowledge, data analysis, and engineering. We do not yet have a team) Tj T* (member with sales experience, and we plan to look for advisors who do.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Milestones and Financials) Tj T* () Tj T* (So far we have defined the core concept, built a working prototype, and registered Vacancy) Tj T* (Atlas LLC. The prototype has been shown to a small number of outside users, including staff at) Tj T* (two city offices and a regional planning group, who gave us feedback on the map and the) Tj T* (scoring. They said the idea was useful, though we do not yet have paying customers or signed) Tj T* (pilot agreements. We also have a website that explains the product.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Our financial position is early. We have spent only small amounts of our own money on hosting) Tj T* (and legal filing. We have not yet generated revenue. Our rough plan is to sign three to five) Tj T* (pilot cities in the next year, convert some of them to paid subscriptions, and reach modest) Tj T* (revenue that covers data and hosting costs by the end of the second year. These projections are) Tj T* (based on assumptions that we have not fully tested, especially the price municipalities are) Tj T* (willing to pay and how quickly they make purchasing decisions.) Tj T* () Tj T* (What We Are Asking For) Tj T* () Tj T* (We are applying to the competition for three things. First, funding to cover data costs,) Tj T* (hosting, and legal advice on data privacy. Second, mentorship from people with experience) Tj T* (selling to local governments, since this is the area where our team is weakest. Third,) Tj T* (introductions to potential pilot cities and data partners. A prize would let us run our first) Tj T* (formal pilots and test whether cities will pay for the product. We are open to feedback on our) Tj T* (model and willing to adjust our approach based on what we learn.) Tj ET
endstream
